import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a3 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BwzYn71E.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Improving the Xircon Module","description":"","frontmatter":{"translationSource":{"title":"优化壤晶模块","archivedAt":"2026-10-31","url":"https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=8uomH9O3s2X12lpR8z1Pf6","scope":"page"},"translationLang":"en","head":[["link",{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://kokobird28144.github.io/endfield-skydoc/improving-the-xircon-module"}],["link",{"rel":"alternate","hreflang":"en","href":"https://kokobird28144.github.io/endfield-skydoc/improving-the-xircon-module"}],["link",{"rel":"alternate","hreflang":"zh-CN","href":"https://kokobird28144.github.io/endfield-skydoc/zh/improving-the-xircon-module"}],["link",{"rel":"alternate","hreflang":"x-default","href":"https://kokobird28144.github.io/endfield-skydoc/improving-the-xircon-module"}]]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"improving-the-xircon-module.md","filePath":"logistics/src/page-8uomH9O3s2X12lpR8z1Pf6.md"}'),a={name:"improving-the-xircon-module.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,u,d){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div class="logistics-content"><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="优化壤晶模块" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="improving-the-adaptive-xircon-module" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="优化自适应壤晶模块" aria-hidden="true"></span><h1 id="improving-the-xircon-module" tabindex="-1">Improving the Xircon Module <a class="header-anchor" href="#improving-the-xircon-module" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Improving the Xircon Module&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Source page ID: <code>8uomH9O3s2X12lpR8z1Pf6</code> | <a href="https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=8uomH9O3s2X12lpR8z1Pf6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open in Tencent Docs</a></p></blockquote><p>The current wish list is mainly:</p><ul><li>Withstand all external disturbances.</li><li>Output all surplus Liquid Xiranite at any Xircon output rate.</li><li>Dispose of externally supplied Sewage without losses.</li><li>Maximize reaction-tank utilization.</li></ul><p>The eventual aim is to fulfill as many of these wishes as possible, perhaps all of them.</p><p><span id="source-block-Dg7Gvh9Er1uguOHTC90b7d"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="抗一切外部扰动" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="resisting-all-external-disturbances" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="introduce-a-water-treatment-unit-to-avoid-self-locking-caused-by-shortage-of-any-input" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="引入污水处理机避免任何原料不足造成的自锁" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="withstanding-all-external-disturbances" tabindex="-1">Withstanding All External Disturbances <a class="header-anchor" href="#withstanding-all-external-disturbances" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Withstanding All External Disturbances&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Xircon module in the current adaptive gross-production blueprint has a problem: a prolonged lack or shortage of Xiranite input can cause a self-locking state that does not clear automatically.</p><p>Changing the priority architecture can avoid the Xiranite shortage, of course. Still, given that this phenomenon exists, automatic recovery after disturbances caused by external bugs is worth investigating.</p><p>Core mechanism of self-locking: self-locking occurs when Xircon Effluent and Sewage both reach 50 while both the Xircon Effluent reaction (Liquid Xiranite + Sewage → Xircon Effluent + inert effluent) and the Xircon reaction (Xircon Effluent + Ferrium Powder → Xircon + Sewage) are underway.</p><p>Core mechanism of automatic unlocking: exporting either Xircon Effluent or Sewage automatically clears the self-lock. If exports are too infrequent, repeated locking and unlocking prevents the maximum rate from being reached.</p><p>Core ways to prevent self-locking: (prevent both materials reaching 50 at once, so one blocks production of the other), or (when both reach 50, withhold Liquid Xiranite—the input for the Xircon Effluent reaction—or withhold its Xiranite or water, so that this reaction does not occur then, and the inventories are no longer both 50 when it does occur), or (when both reach 50, ensure Ferrium Powder is insufficient, preventing the Xircon reaction).</p><p>Self-locking after a Xiranite shortage: Xiranite is insufficient while Xircon Effluent keeps entering. Converting Xircon Effluent produces Sewage until both inventories reach 50. Without the Xircon Effluent reaction, this is not yet self-locked. Supplying Xiranite consumes 1 Sewage to start the Xircon Effluent reaction; completion of the Xircon reaction produces 1 Sewage, returning Sewage to 50, and then consumes 2 Xircon Effluent to start another Xircon reaction. Supplying 2 Xircon Effluent over the next 1 s returns that inventory to 50. Both inventories are now 50, with both reactions underway, causing self-locking. Supplying Sewage instead does not cause this self-lock.</p><p>Self-locking when Xircon output fills up: once Xircon output is blocked, its reaction is fully blocked. With continuous Sewage input, the tank producing Xircon still performs the Xircon Effluent reaction normally, bringing both materials to 50 and naturally entering self-locking. Supplying Xircon Effluent instead does not cause this self-lock.</p><p><span id="source-block-lO5YA2Lxodej3ZjTjFqL43"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="污水大回环" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="a-giant-sewage-loop" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 id="a-huge-sewage-recirculation-loop" tabindex="-1">A Huge Sewage Recirculation Loop!? <a class="header-anchor" href="#a-huge-sewage-recirculation-loop" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A Huge Sewage Recirculation Loop!?&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Keep Sewage flowing so that it can never fill up completely. This prevents the Expanded Crucible&#39;s self-lock caused by both Xircon Effluent and Sewage being full.</p><p>The Sewage flow must also leave enough space for the Xircon reaction. The initial view is that the recirculating flow should be at least the quantity involved in Xircon production.</p><p>Rather than saying it never locks, it may be more accurate to say it can always unlock.</p><p><span class="mark-grey">jnk: Obviously, insufficient flow can cause occasional self-locking and slowdowns; excessive flow can starve the reaction of inputs and also slow it down. Some flow limiting is needed.</span></p><p><img src="/endfield-skydoc/logistics/src/assets/images/img-85e771d93d2e4072.q90-8f2a595dc6a30541.webp" alt="Improving the Xircon Module"></p><div class="logistics-image-caption" data-source-block="PEjMXGVRIQXZ0vHZ9QDXmv"><p>Dark purple: Sewage | Dark green: Inert Xircon Effluent | Cyan: Xircon Effluent | Green: Liquid Xiranite | Blue: Clean Water | Belt Bridge, Depot Unloader</p></div><p><img src="/endfield-skydoc/logistics/src/assets/images/img-6737f121e4c4bb48.q90-6717b9df1a8ecda9.webp" alt="Improving the Xircon Module"></p><p><span id="source-block-jBnSJrOPDTQO0BJbdch9mj"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="结构稳定性相关测试结果" aria-hidden="true"></span><h4 id="structure-stability-test-results" tabindex="-1">Structure-Stability Test Results <a class="header-anchor" href="#structure-stability-test-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Structure-Stability Test Results&quot;">​</a></h4><p>Further results are not yet available.</p><p><span id="source-block-zkScXyZKhCJSPKtTVx2DK2"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="部分壤晶输出下输出所有多余息壤液" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="exporting-all-surplus-liquid-xiranite-over-part-of-the-xircon-output-range" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 id="outputting-all-surplus-liquid-xiranite-at-some-xircon-output-rates" tabindex="-1">Outputting All Surplus Liquid Xiranite at Some Xircon Output Rates <a class="header-anchor" href="#outputting-all-surplus-liquid-xiranite-at-some-xircon-output-rates" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Outputting All Surplus Liquid Xiranite at Some Xircon Output Rates&quot;">​</a></h3><p>by kokobird</p><p><strong>An Endfield Millennium Problem: with three Expanded Crucibles and one Reactor Crucible, taking external Liquid Xiranite, maintain the module&#39;s own Liquid Xiranite production at 90/m when Xircon is blocked, while reducing external Liquid Xiranite input.</strong></p><p><strong>Or, equivalently: four Expanded Crucibles, prioritizing Xircon production and outputting all surplus Liquid Xiranite.</strong></p><p>The key difficulty is the very limited number of facilities and output ports. With three Expanded Crucibles and two Reactor Crucibles, it would be easy. To discuss this problem, you need to:</p><ol><li>Calculate the <strong>allocation between Liquid Xiranite and Xircon Effluent production</strong>, accounting for Purification Units, at different Xircon output rates.</li><li>Know how Xircon blocking propagates, and design a route that <strong>propagates it to the external Liquid Xiranite input</strong>.</li><li>Know <strong>the detailed mechanics of Expanded Crucibles</strong>, such as whether output or reactions take priority, and the conditions for Sewage/effluent self-locking.</li><li>Understand <strong>mixed-pipe mechanics and how to determine blocking</strong>, because the limited ports require mixed-pipe inputs.</li><li>Even account for reaction-phase differences inside Expanded Crucibles, requiring <strong>analysis of production timing</strong>.</li><li>…</li></ol><p>The following image shows one solution. The key is to prevent too much Xircon Effluent entering at once; otherwise it blocks Sewage:</p><p><img src="/endfield-skydoc/logistics/src/assets/images/img-9e89f67dc425f83f.q90-51069d13fbc5accd.webp" alt="Improving the Xircon Module"></p><p>Below is the crap AI churned out about the production-line design above. I&#39;ll come back and fix it when I have time.</p><p><a href="/endfield-skydoc/research-report-adaptive-xircon-module-and-inlet-recirculation-rate">Research Report: Adaptive Xircon Module and Inlet Recirculation Rate Limiting</a></p></div>',1)])])}const g=i(a,[["render",r]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
